 - For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L132)).
 
+## When beforeSession throws
+
+- `beforeSession` runs inside the turn's `try` block, so when it throws an `Error` no later turn hook or provider call runs, `onError(session, error)` fires with the session and the thrown `Error` just like any other orchestrator failure, `afterSession(session)` fires after it, and the rejection still reaches the caller unchanged ([validated by: runs onError with the session and error, then afterSession, skips the rest of the turn, and still rejects](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- `afterSession(session)` keeps its single-argument signature and runs unconditionally in `finally` even when `beforeSession` threw before completing, so a deployer can release resources acquired earlier in `beforeSession`, while `afterSession` cannot assume `beforeSession` finished, that all setup succeeded, or that any user-input or model hook ran; a cleanup hook must check whether each resource was actually allocated before releasing it ([validated by: runs afterSession on processMessageStream when beforeSession throws before completing setup](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L55)).
+
